        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-102224",
        ":question/problem": "What is the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=x-\\sqrt[3]{x}$ at the point $(8,6)?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "This time, we'll use $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ notation. First, we compute the derivative, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x-{x}^{1/3}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {x}^{-2/3} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=8$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=8} & =1-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{8}^{2}}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve is $\\frac{11}{12}.$"
