        ":question/problem": "Find the exact value of the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y=5\\sqrt{x}-10{x}^{3/4}$ at the point $(16,-60).$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "This time, we'll use $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ notation. First, we compute the derivative, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5\\sqrt{x}-10{x}^{3/4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{x}^{1/2}-10{x}^{3/4}) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2}-10\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}{x}^{-1/4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{-1/2}-\\frac{15}{2}{x}^{-1/4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=16$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=16} & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{15}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{25}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at the point $(16,-60)$ is\n\n$$\nm={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=16}=-\\frac{25}{8}.\n$$"
